{"dur":90,"ev":[{"t":1,"type":"voice","id":"v01"},{"t":5.2,"type":"voice","id":"v02"},{"t":16.4,"type":"voice","id":"v03"},{"t":31.3,"type":"voice","id":"m1"},{"t":37.3,"type":"voice","id":"m2"},{"t":43.3,"type":"voice","id":"m3"},{"t":49.9,"type":"voice","id":"m4"},{"t":57.6,"type":"voice","id":"v04"},{"t":63.8,"type":"voice","id":"v05"},{"t":72.2,"type":"voice","id":"v06"},{"t":79,"type":"voice","id":"v07"},{"t":1,"type":"sub","d":3.286,"text":"Once a year, the preserver of the world goes to sleep."},{"t":5.2,"type":"sub","d":9.98,"text":"On a night in the rainy season, Devshayani Ekadashi, Vishnu lies down on the serpent Shesha, on the cosmic ocean, and closes his eyes."},{"t":16.4,"type":"sub","d":4.868,"text":"For four months, the monsoon months, he sleeps. This time is called Chaturmas."},{"t":31.3,"type":"sub","d":1.6,"text":"The rain comes."},{"t":37.3,"type":"sub","d":1.6,"text":"The rivers rise."},{"t":43.3,"type":"sub","d":2.278,"text":"The fields turn green, then gold."},{"t":49.9,"type":"sub","d":1.636,"text":"And the lamps of autumn are lit."},{"t":57.6,"type":"sub","d":5.172,"text":"Then, on Prabodhini Ekadashi, the day of awakening, he opens his eyes."},{"t":63.8,"type":"sub","d":7.398,"text":"Homes celebrate by marrying a sacred basil plant, Tulsi, to Vishnu, under a canopy of sugarcane."},{"t":72.2,"type":"sub","d":2.248,"text":"And the season of weddings begins again."},{"t":79,"type":"sub","d":5.266,"text":"Even asleep, he holds the world. And every year, the world waits for him to wake."},{"t":0.2,"type":"brush","d":2.2,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.8,"pan1":0.8},{"t":1,"type":"sea","d":25},{"t":5.6,"type":"brush","d":3.4,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.6,"pan1":0.6},{"t":9.4,"type":"brush","d":2.6,"g":0.3},{"t":6.6,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":17.4,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":18,"type":"rain","d":9.4,"g":0.6},{"t":20.6,"type":"thunder"},{"t":25,"type":"mist","d":2.2},{"t":27.2,"type":"brush","d":3,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.8,"pan1":0.8},{"t":30.8,"type":"brush","d":1.4,"g":0.35,